<title>UK: London tea auction sees fair demand.</title>
<headline>London tea auction sees fair demand.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-06-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Fair demand was seen at the latest Tea Brokers' Association of London sale but prices were mostly easier.</p>
<p>Coloury medium East Africans lost 3 to 5 pence while other mediums declind 4 to 6 pence with some withdrawals. Plainer Central Africans remained steady.</p>
<p>More demand at firm to dearer rates was seen for offshores, which accounted for 1,200 of 5,400 packages for the day.</p>
</text>
